---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="Terms" description="Draft terms of service for the Identizen hosted services." noindex>
  <div class="container-site max-w-3xl py-16 sm:py-24">
    <article class="prose-idz">
      <p
        class="rounded-md border border-warning-soft bg-warning-soft px-3 py-2 text-sm text-warning-soft-fg"
      >
        Draft. Not yet reviewed by counsel; will be replaced before general availability.
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Terms of service</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-fg-muted">
        These terms cover the services Identizen hosts: the public index, the dashboard, and the
        documentation. The software itself is licensed separately under Apache-2.0.
      </p>

      <h2>The software</h2>
      <p>
        Everything in the Identizen repository is provided under the Apache License 2.0, as is,
        without warranty. Self-hosted deployments are governed by that license alone, not by these
        terms.
      </p>

      <h2>The hosted services</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          The public index is offered free of charge for personal identities, without an
          availability guarantee.
        </li>
        <li>
          Enterprise customers receive the availability, support, and data-processing commitments in
          their order form and DPA, which take precedence over these terms.
        </li>
        <li>
          Do not use the services to attack, spam, or impersonate. We may disable sites or devices
          that do.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your identity</h2>
      <p>
        Your private keys and recovery passphrase are yours alone. We cannot recover a lost
        passphrase for a personal identity and cannot log in as you. Site owners keep their own
        account-recovery paths.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We will post material changes here and, for enterprise customers, notify the account
        contact.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>legal@identizen.com</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Base>
